    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Question\n\nis it possible to make the current displayed buffer not be a part of the picker, and order the opened buffers as most recently used ?\r\nI kinda wanna recreate fzf-lua's buffers implementation, I use <leader><leader> for fast swaps when I am low on screen real estate.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.pick</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">is it possible to make the current displayed buffer not be a part of the picker, and order the opened buffers as most recently used ?<br>\nI kinda wanna recreate fzf-lua's buffers implementation, I use  for fast swaps when I am low on screen real estate.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.pick\nQuestion\nis it possible to make the current displayed buffer not be a part of the picker, and order the opened buffers as most recently used ?\nI kinda wanna recreate fzf-lua's buffers implementation, I use  for fast swaps when I am low on screen real estate.",
